<!-- dashboard.chtpm — db-hq, first real proof of the HQML CSS layer
     (au11-hq/HQML-DESIGN+PLANS.md Phase 1), scoped to Common Events only
     per au11-hq/todo-a12.txt. Rendered by khtpm_hq_render.c (a standalone
     binary, NOT the taskbar's khtpm_strip_parser.c) against dashboard.css.

     Tag vocabulary (own small set, distinct from the taskbar's 5-tag
     ACTIVATE-scope system): window, tabbar, tab, sidebar, item, panel,
     title, text, button. class/id attributes drive CSS selector matching.

     The 15 tabs mirror au11-hq/rpg-maker-database.html's category list
     and ORDER exactly (line 301-316 there - Common Events sits right
     after Tilesets, "Types" and "Terms" are two separate tabs, direct
     correction 2026-08-12); only "Common Events" is wired (its content
     below is real). The other 14 render as a plain placeholder message
     when clicked - see khtpm_hq_render.c's render_placeholder_tab().
     Common Events' sidebar rows are populated at runtime from
     <house_root>/common_events/ (see inject_sidebar_items() in
     khtpm_hq_render.c) - the literal <item> tags below exist only so the
     tag survives an empty directory.

     Task 6 (2026-08-26, direct instruction: "same as how entities events
     works... modeled off rpgmaker mv/mz" - one dialog, sidebar list of
     event slots + the real command editor together, NOT a separate
     spawned window/app) - selecting a sidebar item now opens a REAL,
     embedded events-hq-style editor (page tabs' worth of trigger +
     command list + Add Command + Play) directly in the "panel" below,
     replacing its static placeholder content entirely
     (dbhq_ce_open()/dbhq_ce_inject_panel() in khtpm_core_render.c).
     A prior "Open in Editor" button used to spawn event-ez as a separate
     app for this - that was unwanted drift (event-ez's own entity-side
     launch path had also silently broken, unrelated bug, fixed same
     day) and has been removed; do not re-add it. -->
<!--

     <module> tag added 2026-08-16 (Stage 2d shell/manager split, real
     mechanism this time - direct correction: "explain to me your plan
     and why its different from the tpmos/wraith examples" - first pass
     hardcoded the manager launch into open_db_hq.sh instead of having
     the shell itself parse+launch it). Matches the real reference
     exactly (1.TPMOS_c_+rmmp.0103.0001/projects/wraith-alpha/layouts/
     alpha-shell.chtpm's own <module>path</module> - checked that
     wraith_parser_alpha.c's own module tag ALSO supports a `src="..."`
     attribute form as its primary path, inner-text as fallback - this
     house's own simpler parser only supports attributes, not inner
     text, so `src=` is used here, not a deviation from the real std).
     khtpm_hq_render.c's own main() finds this tag after parsing and
     fork()+execv()s it itself - open_db_hq.sh no longer launches the
     manager directly. -->
<window class="database-window db-hq" label="db-hq">
  <!-- REAL Stage 5 §5d.10 (2026-08-16, khtpm-merge-how2.md) - added
       "db-hq" class alongside the original "database-window" - real,
       data-driven mode detection for khtpm_core_render.+x's own
       g_is_db_hq branch, same convention as taskbar-settings' own
       "swatch-picker" class. "database-window" kept, still used by
       dashboard.css selectors. -->
  <module src="*.monads/*.livedesk-taskbar/ops/+x/khtpm_hq_manager.+x" />
  <tabbar class="tab-bar">
    <tab label="Actors" class="active"/>
    <tab label="Classes"/>
    <tab label="Skills"/>
    <tab label="Items"/>
    <tab label="Weapons"/>
    <tab label="Armors"/>
    <tab label="Enemies"/>
    <tab label="Troops"/>
    <tab label="States"/>
    <tab label="Animations"/>
    <tab label="Tilesets"/>
    <tab label="Common Events"/>
    <tab label="System"/>
    <tab label="Types"/>
    <tab label="Terms"/>
  </tabbar>
  <sidebar id="sidebar" class="sidebar">
    <item label="(loading)"/>
  </sidebar>
  <panel id="common-events-panel" class="settings-block">
    <title class="block-title" label="Common Event"/>
    <text class="event-name" label="(select an event to edit it)"/>
  </panel>
</window>
